# HIP THRUST

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Hip Thrust is a bilateral hip-dominant exercise designed to maximize horizontal force production through powerful hip extension.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most effective exercises for developing gluteal strength, explosive hip extension and sprint-related performance while minimizing spinal loading.

---

# Philosophy

The Hip Thrust isolates one of the most important movement functions for combat athletes:

Powerful hip extension.

Rather than maximizing total body loading, the exercise maximizes force production through the hips while preserving recovery capacity.

CAS selects the Hip Thrust when explosive hip extension provides high transfer to the athlete's performance goals.

