# Success Criteria

The exercise is successful when:

Hip extension strength increases.

Power output improves.

Movement quality remains consistent.

Recovery is appropriate.

Transfer to sport performance is measurable.

---

# Final Principle

The Hip Thrust is not selected because it isolates the glutes.

It is selected because efficient hip extension is one of the fundamental engines of athletic performance.

For many combat athletes, improving horizontal force production provides exceptional transfer while preserving recovery resources.